    "title": "Summer baseball: Jefferson run-rules Waterloo, 14-4 - NewsBreak",
    "text": "WATERLOO — Jefferson's summer baseball team scored six runs in the first inning and surged past host Waterloo 14-4 in five innings on Tuesday. The Eagles' Braxton Thiede finished 3-for-4 with three runs scored and one run driven in. Gavin Berge and Tanner Bergey added two hits apiece while Kairo Leuloff and Keegan DeBlare drove in two runs each. Mason Merz started for Jefferson (9-1) and earned the decision, allowing two earned runs on seven hits in four innings. He struck out five and walked one. Jacob Danielson singled home a run in the Jefferson first while DeBlare added a run-scoring ground out. In the second, Bergey's two-out RBI single to left gave the Eagles a 7-0 lead. Berge's run-scoring double to left in the third pushed Jefferson's margin to 11-0. JEFFERSON 14, WATERLOO 4 (5) Jefferson 632 21 -- 14 11 2 Waterloo 001 12 -- 4 9 3 Leading hitters -- J: Thiede 3x4, Berge 2x2 (2B), Bergey 2x3, Merz (2B) Pitching (ip-h-r-er-bb-so) -- J: Merz W; 4-7-2-2-1-5, DeBlare 1-2-2-1-1-2 Subscribe to Daily Jefferson County Union",
